<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- FOUNDER DECISION PENDING - the data protection keychain needs this, and it needs a
         provisioning profile that only the account holder can mint:

           <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
           <array><string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.realbobcorbin.AgentOasis</string></array>

         Adding it and building with -allowProvisioningUpdates moves the workspace key into
         the data protection keychain, where kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly is
         actually enforced. Without it every such call returns -34018 and the app cannot open
         its own ledger, so KeychainService probes for availability and falls back to the
         legacy keychain rather than failing to start. The fallback is the pre-existing
         behaviour, not a regression - but the stronger protection is NOT in force until this
         entitlement ships. Enabling App Sandbox would also supply an access group, at the
         cost of the SSH connector. -->
</dict>
</plist>
